The classic transform uses the LAST (newest) CompactionRecord in root-first path order and keeps records from `firstKeptEntryId` up to the compaction record. If `firstKeptEntryId` isn't in the path (non-resident), `foundFirstKept` stays false → the entire pre-compaction span is dropped. The `_keptPathResident` fix matches this exactly: check the newest compaction record's `firstKeptEntryId` is on the branch. Consistent with `_applyCompactionTransform`'s "LAST CompactionRecord". Good.

Edge cases in `_keptPathResident`:
1. If `keptId.isEmpty` → returns true. In `_applyCompactionTransform`, an empty firstKeptEntryId means `path[i].id == ''` never matches → foundFirstKept stays false → kept = [compaction] + everything after; all pre-compaction dropped. Hmm wait — kept starts with [compaction], then records before compactionIndex are all dropped (foundFirstKept false). So with empty firstKeptEntryId, transform keeps only the compaction record onward. So "defensive: nothing to wait for" (returns true) is actually consistent with the transform — nothing to wait for since the kept path is just the compaction record itself, which is resident (it matched `found`). OK good.

2. What if `firstKeptEntryId` points at the compaction record itself? Test in equivalence suite uses `"firstKeptEntryId":"c2"` in the exempt test. branch.any((r) => r.id == keptId) — the compaction record itself is on branch → true. Fine.

3. What if the keptId record exists on disk but is on a DIFFERENT branch (not ancestor of the leaf)? Then `_keptPathResident` never returns true and the walk pages to file top. This could over-page: the walk would continue until `!_hasOlder` (everything resident) then return true. On a marathon file with a corrupted/cross-branch firstKeptEntryId, the resume loads the WHOLE file. The budget stop (tokenBudget) is checked... wait — order in the loop:

```dart
if (branch.any(found) && _keptPathResident(branch)) return true;
if (tokenBudget != null) {
  if (estimateProjectedBranchTokens(branch) >= tokenBudget) {
    _trimTokenBudget(branch, tokenBudget);
    return true;
