```

The budget stop STILL applies even when found matched but kept path is not resident. So with a budget set, the over-page is bounded by the budget. Without a budget (CLI resume with boundary reachable — "the found-stop, no budget" per the test), the walk pages to file top — bounded by maxPages (512). maxPages=512 with doubling blocks up to 4096 records/64MB → the walk can read the entire file. For a corrupted session (firstKeptEntryId pointing off-branch), resume reads the whole marathon file (potentially 400MB per comments elsewhere). Previously (old code), the found-stop returned immediately. This is the "boundary unreachable" case the second new test acknowledges: "budget stop wins over kept-path completeness when the boundary is unreachable (issue #503 bounded boot preserved)". But that test passes tokenBudget: 5000. What happens in the CLI path — does the CLI resume call growOlderUntil with a tokenBudget? Let me check the session_commands.dart resume code.

